{"title":"Research","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":""},"headingText":"Research","headingAttr":{"id":"research","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n::: {#top .hero}\n<div class=\"hero-name-row\">\n  <div class=\"hero-name\">Victor Hernandez Martinez</div>\n</div>\n\n::: {.hero-grid}\n::: {.hero-photo}\n![](images/VictorHernandez_HR_closeup.PNG){.profile-image}\n:::\n\n::: {.hero-main}\n<div class=\"hero-subtitle\">Research Economist, Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland</div>\n\nI am an applied microeconomist working in labor and public economics.\n\nMy research studies unemployment, unemployment insurance, wage dynamics, worker displacement, human capital specificity, and the labor market effects of trade and industrial change.\n\nI received my Ph.D. in Economics from the University of Rochester. Before that, I completed a Master's in Economics at the Barcelona School of Economics and a B.A. in Economics at Universidad Carlos III de Madrid.\n:::\n\n::: {.hero-side}\n<div class=\"hero-card\">\n<p class=\"hero-card-label\">Research fields</p>\n<p>Labor Economics<br>Public Economics</p>\n\n<p class=\"hero-card-label\">Affiliation</p>\n<p>Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"files/Victor_Hernandez_Martinez_CV.pdf\" class=\"btn-hero btn-hero-primary btn-hero-card\">Download CV</a></p>\n\n<p class=\"hero-card-label\">Email</p>\n<p><a href=\"mailto:vichdezmtnez@gmail.com\">vichdezmtnez@gmail.com</a></p>\n</div>\n:::\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Working Papers\n\n::: {.research-list}\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title\">An Anatomy of Reemployment Wage Duration Dependence and Its Relationship with the Unemployment Insurance System</div>\n<div class=\"research-links-inline\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1zVLUTs1vukEvwDpIf9seTWgH_T61aop-/view?usp=sharing\">Current Version</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-note research-note-standalone\">Previously circulated as <em>Estimating Duration Dependence on Re-employment Wages When Reservation Wages Are Binding</em>.</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/kaixin-liu/\">Kaixin Liu</a> and Richard Grice</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title\">When Trade Compresses: The Impact of Liberalization on Wage Inequality</div>\n<div class=\"research-links-inline\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10rm1IPBJdvSN2ND_VdeE9ArTJbqH79wd/view?usp=sharing\">Current Version</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With <a href=\"https://nicjkoz.com/\">Nicholas Kozeniauskas</a> and <a href=\"https://romanmerga.com/\">Roman Merga</a></div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title\">Positive Selection During the Unemployed Job Search: Nature of Heterogeneity and Limited Predictability</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/kaixin-liu/\">Kaixin Liu</a></div>\n:::\n:::\n\n### Publications\n\n::: {.research-list}\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head publication-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title publication-title\">The Hedgehog’s Curse: Knowledge Specialization and Displacement Loss</div>\n<div class=\"publication-journal-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.labeco.2025.102769\"><strong><em>Labour Economics</em></strong> (2025), 102769</a><span class=\"research-sep\">·</span><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-wp-202231\">WP</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/robertopinheiropage/\">Roberto Pinheiro</a> and <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/hholter/\">Hans Holter</a></div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head publication-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title publication-title\">Manufacturing Capital-Skill Complementarity: Lessons from the US Shale Boom</div>\n<div class=\"publication-journal-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.euroecorev.2025.105072\"><strong><em>European Economic Review</em></strong> (2025)</a><span class=\"research-sep\">·</span><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-wp-202412\">WP</a></div>\n</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head publication-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title publication-title\">The Value of Unemployment Insurance: Liquidity vs. Insurance Value</div>\n<div class=\"publication-journal-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.labeco.2025.102691\"><strong><em>Labour Economics</em></strong> (2025), 93: 102691</a><span class=\"research-sep\">·</span><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-wp-202216\">WP</a><span class=\"research-sep\">·</span><a href=\"https://www.eeassoc.org/awards/young-economist-award/\">EEA Young Economist Award 2021</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/view/kaixin-liu/\">Kaixin Liu</a></div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head publication-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title publication-title\">Social Distancing Merely Stabilized COVID-19 in the US</div>\n<div class=\"publication-journal-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/sta4.302\"><strong><em>STAT</em></strong> (2020), 9(1): e302</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With Aaron B. Wagner, <a href=\"https://www.elainelhill.com/\">Elaine L. Hill</a>, Sean E. Ryan, Ziteng Sun, Grace Deng, Sourbh Bhadane, Peter Wu, Dongmei Li, Ajay Anand, Jayadev Acharya, and David S. Matteson</div>\n:::\n:::\n\n## Policy {#policy}\n\n::: {.research-list}\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head policy-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title\">Immigration and the Unemployment Rate in 2023-2024</div>\n<div class=\"policy-series-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-ec-202605\"><strong><em>Economic Commentary</em></strong> (2026)</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With Geena Panzitta</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head policy-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title\">Can the IRA and CHIPS Act Reduce Labor Earnings Inequality? Lessons from the US Shale Boom</div>\n<div class=\"policy-series-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-ec-202413\"><strong><em>Economic Commentary</em></strong> (2024)</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With Geena Panzitta</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"research-head policy-head\">\n<div class=\"research-title\">The Effect of Higher Financing Costs on Job Openings and Online Job Postings</div>\n<div class=\"policy-series-inline\"><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.26509/frbc-ec-202309\"><strong><em>Economic Commentary</em></strong> (2023)</a></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"research-meta\">With Adiah Bailey</div>\n:::\n:::\n\n## Teaching {#teaching}\n\n::: {.research-list}\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-primary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-class\">Econometrics</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-course\">Undergraduate, ECO 231W</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-university\">University of Rochester</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-secondary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-role\">Instructor</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-term\">Summer 2020</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-extra\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/19i3LT31Gxx_8hf4zh4AQvP7pbD6dKNZk/view?usp=share_link\">Evaluations</a></div>\n</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-primary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-class\">Econometrics</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-course\">Undergraduate, ECO 231W</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-university\">University of Rochester</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-secondary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-role\">Teaching Assistant</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-term\">Fall 2020, Fall 2019, Fall 2018</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-extra\">Instructor: Prof. Ronni Pavan</div>\n</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-primary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-class\">Econometrics</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-course\">Undergraduate, ECO 231W</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-university\">University of Rochester</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-secondary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-role\">Teaching Assistant</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-term\">Spring 2020, Spring 2019</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-extra\">Instructor: Prof. Kegon Tan</div>\n</div>\n:::\n\n::: {.research-item}\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-primary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-class\">Research in Applied Economics</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-course\">Graduate, ECO 487</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-university\">University of Rochester</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"teaching-row teaching-row-secondary\">\n  <div class=\"teaching-role\">Teaching Assistant</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-term\">Spring 2019</div>\n  <div class=\"teaching-extra\">Instructor: Prof. Ronni Pavan</div>\n</div>\n:::\n:::\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n::: {#top .hero}\n<div class=\"hero-name-row\">\n  <div class=\"hero-name\">Victor Hernandez Martinez</div>\n</div>\n\n::: {.hero-grid}\n::: {.hero-photo}\n![](images/VictorHernandez_HR_closeup.PNG){.profile-image}\n:::\n\n::: {.hero-main}\n<div class=\"hero-subtitle\">Research Economist, Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland</div>\n\nI am an applied microeconomist working in labor and public economics.\n\nMy research studies unemployment, unemployment insurance, wage dynamics, worker displacement, human capital specificity, and the labor market effects of trade and industrial change.\n\nI received my Ph.D. in Economics from the University of Rochester. Before that, I completed a Master's in Economics at the Barcelona School of Economics and a B.A. in Economics at Universidad Carlos III de Madrid.\n:::\n\n::: {.hero-side}\n<div class=\"hero-card\">\n<p class=\"hero-card-label\">Research fields</p>\n<p>Labor Economics<br>Public Economics</p>\n\n<p class=\"hero-card-label\